CNS produces no models on macOS ARM (haddock3 2025.11.0 bundled arm64-darwin
CNS binary runs but writes no rigidbody PDBs, so caprieval fails with
"list index out of range" and all later steps fail; env itself solves).

The haddock3 version is pinned by biobb_haddock 5.3.3 (haddock_biobb 2025.11),
and the CNS binary ships inside the haddock3 PyPI package
(haddock/cns/bin/arm64-darwin.bin). Cause found 2026-11-24 by the macOS notebook
check (docs/testing.md §2.5): the CNS binary links Homebrew's
/opt/homebrew/opt/gcc/lib/gcc/current/libquadmath.0.dylib ("Library not loaded").
The current haddock_biobb recipe (build 1) is linux-64 only on purpose; on a Mac conda
falls back to the old noarch build 0. `brew install gcc` first makes it work (the
notebook passes on macOS, run 45580641026); this lane does not install it yet.

Opts this workflow out of the macOS CI lane only (python-tests.yaml, via the
detect job); the ubuntu-latest lane and all container flavours are unaffected.
Delete this file once CNS works on macOS (biobb_haddock bump to a haddock3
release with a fixed arm64-darwin CNS build).
